<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 2 Best in Slot Gear list for Resto Druids in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Ulduar, Naxxramas, Obsidian Sanctum, and Eye of Eternity. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Restoration Druid Healer Phase 2</h2>The most important gear to acquire in Phase 2 is four pieces of your Tier 8 set <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-78/conquerors-nightsong-regalia">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Conqueror's Nightsong Regalia</span></a> to unlock <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=64760/item-druid-t8-restoration-4p-bonus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Item - Druid T8 Restoration 4P Bonus</span></a>. The power of the instant tick added to your <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48441/rejuvenation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_rejuvenation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rejuvenation</span></a> is greater than the stats of the raw BiS upgrades in each slot.<br/>
<br/>Not only is the addition of an instant tick to your <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48441/rejuvenation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_rejuvenation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rejuvenation</span></a> better healing than the stats of other upgrades, but it improves your raid's survivability by giving Resto Druids something they're sorely missing: A spammable instant heal that can be applied without setup. It's like a mini <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48066/power-word-shield">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_powerwordshield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Power Word: Shield</span></a>. If you've ever had a raid member die to ~1000 overkill before you could heal them, this instant tick might have saved them.<br/>
<br/>The head, shoulders, gloves, and legs are the best slots for your 4pc, but legs/<wbr/>gloves could also be swapped out if you luck into a T8 chest token.<br/>
<br/>Because we need to take two T8 crit pieces without haste to achieve the 4pc set bonus, haste economy is very difficult in Phase 2. It is recommended to stay CF spec (18/<wbr/>0/<wbr/>53) and gem some haste to reach the 1 sec GCD haste cap. If you choose to go for raw BiS upgrades instead of T8 set, you can switch to Thicc Resto (11/<wbr/>0/<wbr/>60) and reach the 856 haste cap. That setup is more focused on 10M raids and tank healing.<br/>
